# Security Rules

Reference: `docs/platform/07_SECURITY_COMPLIANCE_AND_NFR.md`.

- Secrets never enter the repo: no keys, DSNs with tokens, or passwords in code, docs, tests, or `.env.example` (names only). If you find one, report it and do not copy it anywhere.
- Passwords: argon2id only. Tokens/OTPs/reset codes stored hashed; compared with constant-time functions.
- Web auth uses httpOnly `SameSite=Strict` cookies + CSRF header; mobile (Flutter) keeps tokens/PII keys only in `flutter_secure_storage` (Keystore/Keychain). Never store tokens in `localStorage`/AsyncStorage/`shared_preferences`. The pitch app has no backend, so mock credentials are demo-only seed data and never real.
- Every mutating endpoint has `authorize(permission)`; scope filters are applied in repositories — never rely on client-side checks.
- PII (NID, ID proofs, phone, location, signatures) is classified Restricted/Confidential: encrypt where doc 02 §5 says so, redact from logs, exclude from analytics, respect retention jobs.
- Files: presigned uploads only, MIME sniffed server-side, AV-scanned before download, private buckets. Never serve user files from the API process.
- Validate all external input with zod (body, query, params, headers, socket payloads, job data).
- No `eval`, no dynamic `require`, no shelling out with user input; raw SQL only via tagged templates.
- Rate-limit auth, OTP and upload endpoints per doc 07; return generic messages for login failures.
- Dependency changes: run `npm audit`; do not add packages with known critical CVEs or unmaintained forks.
- E-signature and audit paths are tamper-evident: hash chains and `audit_logs` are append-only — never add update/delete code paths for them.
